 Download Node Exporter

Run these commands on every node.

cd /opt

sudo wget https://github.com/prometheus/node_exporter/releases/download/v1.8.2/node_exporter-1.8.2.linux-amd64.tar.gz

Extract:

sudo tar -xzf node_exporter-1.8.2.linux-amd64.tar.gz

sudo mv node_exporter-1.8.2.linux-amd64 node_exporter

Verify:

ls /opt/node_exporter

You should see:

LICENSE
NOTICE
node_exporter

Step 1: Create a dedicated user
sudo useradd --no-create-home --shell /bin/false node_exporter

Verify:

id node_exporter
Step 2: Give ownership
sudo chown -R node_exporter:node_exporter /opt/node_exporter
Step 3: Create a systemd service
sudo nano /etc/systemd/system/node_exporter.service

Paste:

[Unit]
Description=Prometheus Node Exporter
After=network.target

[Service]
User=node_exporter
Group=node_exporter
Type=simple
ExecStart=/opt/node_exporter/node_exporter

Restart=always
RestartSec=5

[Install]
WantedBy=multi-user.target

Save:

Ctrl + O
Enter
Ctrl + X
Step 4: Reload systemd
sudo systemctl daemon-reload
Step 5: Enable service
sudo systemctl enable node_exporter
Step 6: Start service
sudo systemctl start node_exporter
Step 7: Verify
sudo systemctl status node_exporter

You should see something like:

Active: active (running)
Step 8: Check listening port
sudo ss -tulnp | grep 9100

Expected:

LISTEN 0 4096 *:9100
